/* Page continuity, "Drawn, then built" (2026-10-27): index.html, case-study.html and the standalone
 * project-3d.html move into each other instead of cutting.
 *
 * - Cross-document View Transitions: the outgoing page fades out (0-160 ms) as the incoming one
 *   fades in (80-240 ms), develop ease cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1), so two pages of text never sit
 *   on top of each other.
 * - Card <-> stage: a click (or Enter) on a project card morphs its cover into the detail page's
 *   stage (400 ms, same ease). Back, or the detail page's "Back to projects" link, morphs the stage
 *   into that project's card, after this tab's scroll position on the homepage is restored. The
 *   card cover and the stage poster are the same frame-0 render (3:2), so the two snapshots are
 *   fitted to stay registered through the morph: the card's snapshot contains, the stage's covers.
 *   The morph multiplies onto the page, so the object travels, not its white box (no neighbouring
 *   card or text is covered on the way), and the card's hover controls stay out of it.
 * - The morph is the arrival: a detail page entered through a card morph skips its line-drawing
 *   arrival. Before the first frame this file sets html[data-vt-entry="morph"] (the page's CSS
 *   keeps the poster at full strength) and fires a "kw-vt-morph" event on window
 *   (project-case-3d.js and case-study.js end an arrival that has not started). Deep links,
 *   refreshes, new tabs and any entry without a morph still draw.
 * - A morph happens only when both ends are on screen and the window is landscape (portrait screens
 *   magnify the stage and phones open it below the fold): the card (>= 25 % of its cover when it is
 *   left, >= 50 % after the return) and the stage (>= 96 px of it when it is left; >= 50 % of its
 *   height when it is entered, so the cover never lands as a sliver at the bottom edge after flying
 *   over the hero text). Otherwise the pages only fade, and a named end without a partner fades with
 *   the page (160 ms, the inline CSS), so it never lingers over the new title.
 * - A window under 1040 px tall skips the forward morph before it pays for it: the stage is 100svh
 *   - 155 px tall and starts at least 614 px down, so half of it needs about 1073 px (measured
 *   2026-11-04, 16 projects: at most 49 % at 1680x1050, 50 % first at 1920x1080). The card is not
 *   named and no flag is written, so the detail page has no hold on its first frame: the crossfade
 *   starts about 60 ms sooner, and a pointer move has that much less time to abort it (see below).
 * - Leaving a detail page for the homepage: the stage is named only for a return to this project's
 *   card (no fragment, or #project-<this key>). Any other homepage fragment (#work, #contact, or the
 *   card with the stage off screen) writes a "crossfade" flag instead: the homepage is held until
 *   parsed and lands on the fragment target, instantly, before its first frame (no hero frame, no
 *   smooth scroll afterwards).
 * - Destinations without the opt-in (the studio, 404, the resume PDF, ?vt=off) get no transition:
 *   the inline bootstrap skips it in pageswap (capturing, so it also covers a click before this file
 *   has loaded), and this file leaves a skipped transition alone. Every view-transition promise
 *   this file touches has a rejection handler. The same skip applies on a connection that reports
 *   slow (below).
 * - One rejection no page code can reach: when input (a pointer move, a key press) reaches a
 *   destination that is still render-blocked by its style sheets or #kw-vt-hold, Chromium drops the
 *   transition and rejects an internal promise with InvalidStateError "Transition was aborted because
 *   of invalid state. Page already revealed", before pagereveal fires (seen 2026-11-04, also on two
 *   script-free pages with a render-blocking script). The navigation itself is unharmed: it lands
 *   with a hard cut, pagereveal.viewTransition is null, and the arrival runs as on a deep link. Two
 *   things keep the rejection out of the console (both generated by head-block.cjs):
 *   - script#kw-vt-filter, the first script of the page, right after <meta charset>: an
 *     unhandledrejection listener that calls preventDefault on exactly that name and message; any other
 *     rejection is still reported. It can run after about 300 compressed bytes (the bootstrap: 2-3 KB),
 *     so it arrives with the response headers (one probe of the live CDN, 2026-11-05: first body bytes
 *     within 1 ms of the headers, at least 2.2 KB of them).
 *   - The rejection can still come first when the document's bytes trickle in, and no script of that
 *     page can catch it then. So the page being left skips the transition in pageswap when the connection
 *     reports slow: effectiveType slow-2g, 2g or 3g (the case-study.js test; an RTT of 272 ms or more) or
 *     a downlink under .7 Mbps (a low-RTT link reports 4g however thin it is). Those visits get the hard
 *     cut they would get with no transitions at all.
 *   What is left: the headers arrive alone, the first body packet is late, the connection reports fast,
 *   and input lands in that gap. No page code can reach that; the console shows the line, the visitor
 *   nothing.
 *
 * Split, so nothing here delays a first paint that needs no morph:
 * - Inline at the top of each page's <head>, before its style sheets (identical on all three pages):
 *   the transition CSS (style#kw-vt-style, the opt-in inside a prefers-reduced-motion media query)
 *   and a bootstrap that runs at once (it never waits for the CSS, so neither the parser nor the
 *   page's own deferred scripts are held up). It removes the style when transitions are off (?vt=off,
 *   the studio's iframe, no browser support), decides the hold, and loads this file: at once with
 *   high priority on a held page, otherwise after the load event (or 5 s), at low priority, so its
 *   bytes never compete with the first paint. Inside the studio's iframe it loads nothing.
 * - After the page's own classic deferred scripts: an inert render-blocking script#kw-vt-hold
 *   (deferred, empty). The bootstrap removes it as soon as it is parsed, unless the first frame would
 *   be wrong without it: a card morph into a detail page whose stage is not built yet (case-study.js
 *   is deferred), or a back/forward return to the homepage that must be parsed before the visitor's
 *   scroll position is restored. The hold ends when this file sees the far end exist, when the hold's
 *   own deferred turn comes (after case-study.js), or at the bootstrap's 1 s cap.
 * - This file names the ends in pageswap/pagereveal, restores the scroll position (or performs a
 *   fragment link's scroll) and adds the prefetch rules. On a held page it has arrived long before
 *   the hold ends (requested first, at high priority); if it ever arrives later, the page fades with
 *   the inline CSS alone and its arrival draws. If the far end's image has not decoded yet, the
 *   morph keeps the outgoing image as its stand-in and cross-fades only once it has (IMAGE_MS at
 *   most), so it never lands on an empty frame.
 * - Intent during a transition (pointer, touch, wheel, key, a hidden tab) ends it at once.
 * - Prefetch: speculation rules prefetch (documents only, never prerender, which would boot WebGL;
 *   never the studio) case-study.html?project=* and project-3d.html?project=* links, eagerness
 *   "moderate" (hover or press). Skipped with data saver or a 2g connection; off with ?prefetch=off.
 * - A view-transition-name lives on one element for the length of one transition only.
 * - QA: window.__vt = { enabled, reason, prefetch, hold, reveal, swap } (window.__vtBoot: bootstrap).
 */
(() => {
  "use strict";

  const w = window, d = document, root = d.documentElement;
  const boot = w.__vtBoot || { on: false, hold: "" };
  const QA = (w.__vt = { enabled: false, reason: "", prefetch: "", hold: null, reveal: null, swap: null });
  // The hold sits after the page's deferred scripts: this file (loaded early, async) may run before
  // the parser reaches it, so it is looked up when needed.
  const holdEl = () => d.getElementById("kw-vt-hold");
  const release = (why) => {
    const hold = holdEl();
    if (!hold) return;
    hold.remove();
    QA.hold = { ms: Math.round(performance.now() - (boot.t0 || 0)), why };
  };
  try {
    setup();
  } catch (error) {
    QA.reason = `error: ${error && error.message}`;
    release("error");
  }

  function setup() {
    const query = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    let framed = true;
    try { framed = w.top !== w; } catch (e) { framed = true; }
    if (framed) { QA.reason = QA.prefetch = "framed"; return; }   // the studio shows project-3d.html in an iframe

    const store = {
      get(k) { try { return sessionStorage.getItem(k); } catch (e) { return null; } },
      set(k, v) { try { sessionStorage.setItem(k, v); } catch (e) { /* storage blocked: no morph */ } },
      del(k) { try { sessionStorage.removeItem(k); } catch (e) { /* ignore */ } },
    };
    const kindOf = (path) => /\/(index\.html)?$/.test(path) ? "home"
      : /\/(case-study|project-3d)\.html$/.test(path) ? "detail" : "";
    const here = kindOf(location.pathname);

    // ---- prefetch (documents only) ----
    QA.prefetch = (() => {
      if (query.get("prefetch") === "off") return "kill-switch";
      if (!(w.HTMLScriptElement && HTMLScriptElement.supports && HTMLScriptElement.supports("speculationrules"))) return "unsupported";
      const c = navigator.connection;
      if (c && (c.saveData || /^(slow-2g|2g)$/.test(c.effectiveType || ""))) return "save-data";
      const rules = d.createElement("script");
      rules.type = "speculationrules";
      rules.textContent = JSON.stringify({ prefetch: [{
        source: "document",
        where: { or: [{ href_matches: "/case-study.html?project=*" }, { href_matches: "/project-3d.html?project=*" }] },
        eagerness: "moderate",
      }] });
      d.head.append(rules);
      return "on";
    })();

    // ---- transitions (the inline bootstrap decided whether this page takes part) ----
    if (!boot.on) { QA.reason = boot.reason || "off"; return; }
    QA.enabled = true;

    const NAME = "kw-morph";
    const FLAG = "kw-vt";          // the outgoing page's morph, read (and removed) by the next page
    const SCROLL = "kw-vt-y:";     // + history entry key: where this homepage entry was left
    const IMAGE_MS = 600;          // longest a morph keeps its stand-in for an image still decoding
    const STAGE_PX = 96, STAGE_ENTER = 0.5, CARD_LEAVE = 0.25, CARD_RETURN = 0.5, PORTRAIT = 0.8;
    const STAGE_WINDOW = 1040;     // shorter than this, no project's stage can land half on screen
    const landscape = () => innerWidth / innerHeight > PORTRAIT;
    const quiet = (vt) => { [vt.ready, vt.finished, vt.updateCallbackDone].forEach((p) => { if (p) p.catch(() => {}); }); };

    let named = null;
    function unname() {
      if (!named) return;
      named.style.removeProperty("view-transition-name");
      named.removeAttribute("data-vt-named");
      if (!named.getAttribute("style")) named.removeAttribute("style");
      named = null;
    }
    function name(el) {
      unname();
      el.style.viewTransitionName = NAME;
      el.setAttribute("data-vt-named", "");   // its card controls stay out of the snapshot
      named = el;
    }
    // How much of an element is on screen: { px: visible height, share: of its height }.
    function seen(el) {
      const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
      const across = Math.min(r.right, innerWidth) - Math.max(r.left, 0);
      const px = across > 0 ? Math.max(0, Math.min(r.bottom, innerHeight) - Math.max(r.top, 0)) : 0;
      return { px, share: r.height > 0 ? px / r.height : 0 };
    }
    const stageOf = (key) => {
      const host = d.querySelector(".case-animation-host[data-project]");
      return host && (!key || host.dataset.project === key) ? host.querySelector(":scope > .card-media") : null;
    };
    const cardOf = (key) => {
      const card = key ? d.getElementById(`project-${key}`) : null;
      return card && card.matches(".project-card:not(.is-hidden)") ? card.querySelector(".card-media") : null;
    };
    const pageKey = () => location.origin + location.pathname + location.search;
    const readFlag = () => {
      try {
        const flag = JSON.parse(store.get(FLAG) || "null");
        return flag && flag.to === pageKey() && Date.now() - flag.at < 15000 ? flag : null;
      } catch (e) { return null; }
    };
    const savedY = () => {
      const entry = w.navigation && navigation.currentEntry;
      const y = entry && entry.key ? Number(store.get(SCROLL + entry.key) ?? NaN) : NaN;
      return Number.isFinite(y) ? y : null;
    };
    // A homepage reached by a link with a fragment: land on its target now, instantly (the page's
    // html { scroll-behavior: smooth } is overridden for this one call), scroll-margin included.
    // Not on back/forward, where the visitor's own position wins.
    const toFragment = () => {
      if (here !== "home" || location.hash.length < 2) return false;
      const act = w.navigation && navigation.activation;
      if (act && act.navigationType === "traverse") return false;
      let target = null;
      try { target = d.getElementById(decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1))); } catch (e) { target = null; }
      if (!target) return false;
      const was = root.style.scrollBehavior;
      root.style.scrollBehavior = "auto";
      target.scrollIntoView({ block: "start", behavior: "instant" });
      root.style.scrollBehavior = was;
      if (!root.getAttribute("style")) root.removeAttribute("style");
      return true;
    };

    // ---- the held first frame: end it as soon as the far end is ready ----
    if (boot.hold && !boot.capped) {
      const incoming = readFlag();
      let watch = null;
      const done = (why) => {
        if (watch) watch.disconnect();
        watch = null;
        d.removeEventListener("readystatechange", check);
        release(why);
      };
      function check() {
        // Ended elsewhere (the bootstrap's 1 s cap, or the hold's own deferred run): stop watching.
        if (boot.capped || (d.readyState !== "loading" && !holdEl())) { done("released"); return; }
        if (boot.hold === "stage" ? Boolean(incoming && stageOf(incoming.key)) : d.readyState !== "loading") {
          if (boot.hold === "parsed" && incoming) toFragment();   // the first frame is already on the target
          done(boot.hold);
        }
      }
      if (boot.hold === "stage" && !incoming) done("no-flag");
      else {
        watch = new MutationObserver(check);
        watch.observe(d, { childList: true, subtree: true });
        d.addEventListener("readystatechange", check);
        check();
      }
    }

    // ---- leaving: name the end that is on screen and tell the next page ----
    addEventListener("pageswap", (event) => {
      unname();
      const act = event.activation, vt = event.viewTransition;
      const info = (QA.swap = { at: Math.round(performance.now()), vt: Boolean(vt), type: act ? act.navigationType : "", to: act && act.entry ? act.entry.url : "", result: "" });
      const entry = w.navigation && navigation.currentEntry;
      if (here === "home" && entry && entry.key) store.set(SCROLL + entry.key, String(Math.round(scrollY)));
      if (vt) quiet(vt);
      // Skipped by the inline bootstrap: the destination has no opt-in (studio, 404, PDF, ?vt=off) or the connection is slow.
      if (vt && boot.skipped === event) { info.result = boot.slow ? "skipped-slow" : "skipped-optout"; return; }
      if (!vt || !act || !act.entry || !act.entry.url) { info.result = "no-transition"; return; }
      const to = new URL(act.entry.url, location.href);
      if (to.origin !== location.origin) { info.result = "cross-origin"; return; }
      const toKind = kindOf(to.pathname);
      let el = null, dir = "", key = "";
      if (here === "home" && toKind === "detail") {
        key = to.searchParams.get("project") || "";
        const card = cardOf(key);
        // A portrait window never morphs into the stage (the detail page applies the same rule), and
        // a short one cannot land it: the card is not named, it fades with the page instead of
        // lingering over the next one, and the detail page holds nothing for a morph that never comes.
        if (card && seen(card).share >= CARD_LEAVE && landscape() && innerHeight >= STAGE_WINDOW) { el = card; dir = "to-stage"; }
      } else if (here === "detail" && toKind === "home") {
        const host = d.querySelector(".case-animation-host[data-project]");
        key = host ? host.dataset.project : "";
        const stage = stageOf(key);
        const hash = to.hash.length > 1 ? to.hash : "";
        // Only a return to this project's card morphs, and only from a landscape window with the
        // stage on screen (portrait: the plain root crossfade, no ghost of the stage over the card).
        if ((!hash || hash === `#project-${key}`) && stage && seen(stage).px >= STAGE_PX && landscape()) { el = stage; dir = "to-card"; }
        // Any other homepage fragment: nothing is named, but the homepage is held until parsed and
        // lands on the fragment before its first frame (see toFragment).
        else if (hash) dir = "crossfade";
      }
      if (!dir) { info.result = "crossfade"; return; }
      if (el) name(el);
      store.set(FLAG, JSON.stringify({ to: to.origin + to.pathname + to.search, key, dir, at: Date.now() }));
      info.result = dir;
      info.key = key;
    });

    // ---- arriving (before the first frame): restore, measure, name the other end ----
    addEventListener("pagereveal", (event) => {
      unname();
      delete root.dataset.vtMorph;
      const flag = readFlag();
      store.del(FLAG);
      const vt = event.viewTransition;
      const act = w.navigation && navigation.activation;
      const info = (QA.reveal = { at: Math.round(performance.now()), vt: Boolean(vt), type: act ? act.navigationType : "", dir: flag ? flag.dir : "", result: "" });
      // Back or forward to the homepage: the visitor's own scroll position before anything else
      // (a no-op after a back/forward-cache restore, which keeps it).
      if (here === "home" && act && act.navigationType === "traverse") {
        const y = savedY();
        info.scrollAt = Math.round(scrollY);
        if (y !== null && Math.abs(scrollY - y) > 1 && y <= root.scrollHeight - innerHeight + 1) scrollTo({ top: y, behavior: "instant" });
        info.scrollTo = Math.round(scrollY);
      } else if (here === "home" && vt && location.hash.length > 1) {
        // A link to the homepage with a fragment (a detail page's "Back to projects", index.html
        // #project-<key> or #work): the browser scrolls to it only after this first frame, so do
        // the same fragment scroll now (instant, scroll-margin included), or the first frame is the
        // top of the page and the card is not on screen to be found.
        toFragment();
        info.fragmentTo = Math.round(scrollY);
      }
      if (!vt) { info.result = "no-transition"; return; }
      quiet(vt);
      // Any intent ends the transition at once (the page underneath is already today's page).
      const stop = () => vt.skipTransition();
      const hidden = () => { if (d.hidden) stop(); };
      const INTENT = ["pointerdown", "touchstart", "wheel", "keydown"];
      INTENT.forEach((type) => addEventListener(type, stop, { capture: true, passive: true }));
      d.addEventListener("visibilitychange", hidden);
      const cleanup = () => {
        INTENT.forEach((type) => removeEventListener(type, stop, { capture: true }));
        d.removeEventListener("visibilitychange", hidden);
        unname();
        delete root.dataset.vtMorph;
        info.finishedAt = Math.round(performance.now());
      };
      vt.finished.then(cleanup, cleanup);
      // A named end on the outgoing page with no partner here just fades with the page.
      root.dataset.vtMorph = "none";
      if (!flag || flag.dir === "crossfade") { info.result = "crossfade"; return; }
      let el = null;
      if (flag.dir === "to-stage" && here === "detail") {
        const stage = stageOf(flag.key);
        const s = stage ? seen(stage) : null;
        info.stage = s ? Math.round(s.px) : -1;
        info.stageShare = s ? Math.round(s.share * 100) / 100 : -1;
        if (!stage) info.result = "no-stage";
        else if (!landscape()) info.result = "portrait";
        // Morph only when it can land on screen: half the stage at least, else a calm crossfade.
        else if (s.share < STAGE_ENTER) info.result = "stage-offscreen";
        else el = stage;
      } else if (flag.dir === "to-card" && here === "home") {
        const card = cardOf(flag.key);
        if (!card) info.result = "no-card";
        else if (seen(card).share < CARD_RETURN) info.result = "card-offscreen";
        else el = card;
      } else info.result = "mismatch";
      if (!el) return;
      name(el);
      root.dataset.vtMorph = flag.dir;
      // The far end's image may still be loading or decoding (the stage poster is a larger file than
      // the card's cover; a returning card's cover is lazy). Until it has decoded (IMAGE_MS at most)
      // the morph keeps the outgoing image at full strength as its stand-in, and only then
      // cross-fades, so it never lands on an empty frame. An image already decoded by the time the
      // transition starts changes nothing.
      const image = el.querySelector(":scope > img");
      if (image) {
        let ready = false;
        const loaded = image.complete ? Promise.resolve() : new Promise((resolve) => {
          image.addEventListener("load", resolve, { once: true });
          image.addEventListener("error", resolve, { once: true });
        });
        const decoded = loaded.then(() => (image.naturalWidth && image.decode ? image.decode() : undefined)).then(() => { ready = true; }, () => { ready = true; });
        vt.ready.then(() => {
          if (ready) return;
          info.standIn = true;
          const pair = d.getAnimations().filter((a) => a.effect
            && [`::view-transition-old(${NAME})`, `::view-transition-new(${NAME})`].includes(a.effect.pseudoElement));
          pair.forEach((a) => a.pause());
          let played = false;
          const play = () => {
            if (played) return;
            played = true;
            info.standInMs = Math.round(performance.now() - info.at);
            pair.forEach((a) => { try { a.play(); } catch (e) { /* transition already over */ } });
          };
          decoded.then(play);
          setTimeout(play, IMAGE_MS);
        }, () => {});
      }
      info.result = flag.dir;
      info.key = flag.key;
      if (flag.dir === "to-stage") {
        // The morph is this page's arrival: no drawing (project-case-3d.js, case-study.js).
        root.dataset.vtEntry = "morph";
        w.dispatchEvent(new Event("kw-vt-morph"));
      }
    });
  }
})();
